**WHEREAS**, the League desires to establish a professional soccer league known as the National Professional Soccer League (the "NPSL"), and the Team Owners wish to participate in the League subject to the terms and conditions set forth herein;

**NOW, THEREFORE**, in consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements contained herein, the parties agree as follows:

**ARTICLE I: LEAGUE FORMATION AND OPERATION**

**1.1 Formation of the League**  
The League shall be established as a professional soccer league consisting of not less than eight (8) teams, each owned and operated by the Team Owners. Each owner shall have equal voting rights in the decision-making processes of the League as defined in the League's bylaws.

**1.2 League Structure**  
The League shall consist of two conferences: the Eastern Conference and the Western Conference. Each conference shall have a minimum of four (4) teams. The League shall oversee the scheduling of matches, playoff formats, and rule enforcement.

